Remove -Werror from the AWS-LC compiler flags.

AWS-LC adds -Werror for GCC and Clang unconditionally, so a false positive warning of a newer compiler
or of a build with sanitizers (for example GCC 13 -O3 with -fsanitize=address,undefined: stringop-overflow,
array-bounds, format-truncation) fails the build of every project that uses AWS-LC as a dependency.
-Werror in the check of supported compiler flags is kept.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -798,7 +798,7 @@
       set(C_CXX_FLAGS "${C_CXX_FLAGS} -Wno-c11-extensions")
     endif()
   endif()
-  set(C_CXX_FLAGS "${C_CXX_FLAGS} -Werror -Wformat=2 -Wsign-compare -Wmissing-field-initializers -Wwrite-strings")
+  set(C_CXX_FLAGS "${C_CXX_FLAGS} -Wformat=2 -Wsign-compare -Wmissing-field-initializers -Wwrite-strings")
 
   # GCC 8.x added a warning called -Wcast-function-type to the -Wextra umbrella.
   # Also suppress for all clang versions supporting this warning.
